On Mar 6, 11:56 am, purple arcanist <ejg_...@yahoo.com> wrote:
> I think that prayer should be changed in nethack.
> First, if the player recieves a boon, they should be able to choose
> from a list of general choices for it, rather than having it chosen at
> random.
> Second, crowning should be more beneficial to the player, since as of
> now, it is only really good for a wizard to get crowned.
>
> I will post more ideas later. ;)

There are two ways to look at this suggestion: from the standpoint of
how it works in the game's world, and how it affects the play.

Gods, being gods, generally assume they know better than their
followers what they need, so getting a choice from a list is kind of
out of character.

As for crowning, I am not siding with the others in saying it
shouldn't be made more useful.  The idea that it is intended to be a
negative benefit, I think, is an assumed attitude based off of a
statement in a spoiler and the present game effect.  Crowning is one
of the coolest ideas in Nethack: it gives the player a title, affects
shopkeeper greetings, and gets noted in the Final Attributes list.  I
don't think it should be dismissed as mostly a way to make prayer
harder.  This is a situation, I would say, of people defending
something just because it is so, rather than examining what it should
be.

I don't think the game should be made easier generally, and the way
the game is balanced right now making crowning more valuable would
require both making it less frequent and finding a different way to
balance prayer.  But the basic idea is still good.

